rl":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Okay, but which \"color map\"? And how is it applied? It's very meaningless without further context. Indeed, as brought up in the PR's description, the color map is set up by the editor.\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/fa6cad230f638d65a5a897008c5fc512edc237ad/editor/themes/editor_color_map.cpp#L44-L57\n\nSpecifically, it's first used when ResourceImporterTexture's `editor/convert_colors_with_editor_theme` is set to `true`.\n\nThe point is, the description is too vague, but perhaps linking its corresponding property in ResourceImporterTexture may be enough, as as that description provides a good explanation for it.\n\n```suggestion\n\t\t\tIf set, a predefined color map is applied to the image. Used when [member ResourceImporterTexture.editor/convert_colors_with_editor_theme] is [code]true[/code].\n```\nor, heavily taking from _that_ description:\n```suggestion\n\t\t\tIf set, converts the image's colors to match [url=$DOCS_URL/engine_details/editor/creating_icons.html]Godot's own color palette for editor icons[/url]. See also [member ResourceImporterTexture.editor/convert_colors_with_editor_theme].\n```","created_at":"2026-05-25T16:29:10Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T16:29:37Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119612#discussion_r3299142620","pull_request_url":"https://ap